{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update34.json\",\"summary\":\"Submitted a two-voter probe that bounds the configuration-recovery claim, which until now showed only that a node recovering without a configuration never becomes a candidate. The new test in draft/assurance_multi_test.go builds a two-voter group, makes B the leader, commits until A's store reports a non-zero persisted commit index, restarts A with the replay enabled (A tracks no configuration), then restarts B so that it must campaign and can only win with A's vote; the harness samples A's state while B campaigns. One admission event records the empty tracked configuration alongside the two-voter group size, and one comparison asserts that the peer is still elected - because a majority of two is both members, B's leadership shows A granted its vote, which separates a node that cannot be a candidate from one that cannot participate. Local construction feedback reproduced the outcome twice: A tracked index 0 with no members and showed zero candidate samples, while B reached Leader in both runs. The retained receipt is requested; its citation in the account of that question is the next step if the run allows.\"}"}}
